[0.030, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[2m87 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m87 \u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2m    *   `airwolf`, `kitt`, `starfury` (the specific confidential SRL projects he exfiltrated)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m88 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m88 \u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2m3.  **Pre-Existing USB Pairing:** The external USB drives D: (`SRL IRT`), E: (`Homework`), and F: (`CRIMSON2`) used for exfiltration were first connected/migrated to the Surface system on November 1, 2020, well before Fred left on vacation. This confirms the physical devices belonged to Fred and were already paired with his machine.\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m89 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m89 \u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2m\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m90 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m## Recovered Browser & System Credentials\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m91 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33mThrough a combination of Dissect's automated credential decryption and LSA secret analysis, we successfully recovered plaintext passwords from the system, providing absolute confirmation of Fred's identity and intent:\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m92 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m1.  **Personal Email & Microsoft Account:**\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m93 \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Username:** `redguard.cobra@gmail.com` (personal/insider threat email)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m94 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Username:** `fred.rocba@outlook.com` (personal MS account)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m95 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Username:** `fred.rocba@gmail.com` (personal primary email)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m96 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Plaintext Password:** `C0bracommand` (Decrypted from Chrome/Edge `Login Data`)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m97 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Significance:** Fred utilized the password `C0bracommand` (referencing his \"Cobra\" alias) across all his personal accounts (including Google, Microsoft, Netflix, Amazon, and Facebook), establishing undeniable proof of ownership of the `redguard.cobra@gmail.com` exfiltration account.\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m98 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m2.  **SRL Corporate Domain Account:**\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m99 \u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Username:** `SHIELDBASE\\frocba` (SRL corporate account)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m100\u001b[0m"]
[0.000, "o", " |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Plaintext Password:** `Big-Purple-Truck` (Decrypted from Windows LSA secrets / `RASDIALPARAMS` cache)\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m101\u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m    *   **Significance:** This confirms the exact credentials Fred used to authenticate to the SRL corporate domain and VPN.\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m   \u001b[0m \u001b[2m102\u001b[0m |\u001b[33m+\u001b[0m\u001b[33m\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m90 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m103\u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2m## Email Archive Exfiltration\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m91 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m104\u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2mAt 05:39:11 on November 14, 2020, Fred deleted his local Outlook backup file `backup.pst` (size 20.5 MB), moving it to the Recycle Bin. Exactly 11 seconds later (at 05:39:22), he created and copied `SRL-EMAIL-EXPORT.pst` directly to his Google Drive folder (`G:\\My Drive\\STARK-RESEARCH-LABS FOLDER\\Exported-PST\\`). He then opened this Google Drive PST file in Outlook to verify its contents, updating his Outlook registry keys (`LastCorruptStore`) at 06:09:16 to point directly to the exfiltrated Google Drive path.\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[2m92 \u001b[0m \u001b[2m105\u001b[0m |\u001b[2m \u001b[0m\u001b[2m\r\n\u001b["]
